Three command-line tools for Beeb enthusiasts to view BBC Micro files and disk images on their Windows PC. Supports plain text, BBCode, or HTML output, and file extraction from disk images. With one command you can [b][i]produce a master "catalog" of all your disk images in minutes[/i][/b].

[list]
[*] [b]BBCBasicToText[/b] — display a tokenized, binary BBC Micro BASIC file as [color=green][b]text[/b][/color], [color=darkred][b]HTML[/b][/color], or [color=darkcyan][b]BBCode[/b][/color].
[*] [b]BBCDataFileToText[/b] — show BBC PRINT# type data files as text, HTML, or BBCode.
[*] [b]BBCReadDiskImage[/b] — display *CAT-style output of .DSD or .SSD disk images, with the ability to export files individually and dump sectors.
[/list]

I wrote them as console applications and posted links to the initial versions on this board back in 2023. I've had a bit of free time, so I revisited them, fixing some bugs and making the utilities available from the [i]Microsoft Store[/i] so they've been scanned, tested and signed.

[size=150][b]BBCBasicToText[/b][/size]

This utility displays a tokenized, binary BBC Micro BASIC file as text, HTML, or BBCode for bulletin board posts. If there is "hidden data" after the BASIC program, that will be displayed in hex, as will control characters.

[img]https://karaottewell.github.io/KLO-Software/Screenshot_BBCBasicToTextExample.png[/img]

[size=150][b]BBCDataFileToText[/b][/size]

Show BBC PRINT#-type data files as text, HTML, or BBCode, with hex and ASCII dump options.

[img]https://karaottewell.github.io/KLO-Software/Screenshot_BBCDataFileToTextExample.png[/img]

This can actually be used as a "hex dump" program for any PC file. I have

[code]
doskey hex=BBCDataFileToText --hex $*
[/code]

defined in my command terminals for that reason.

[b][i]> hex  binaryfile.bin binaryfile.bbcode[/i][/b]
[color=DarkGray]
